{"author":{"avatar":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15904127?v=4","date":"2017-08-26T15:54:02Z","email":"karokidii@gmail.com","login":"kd-11","name":"kd-11"},"committer":{"avatar":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15904127?v=4","date":"2017-08-26T18:53:54Z","email":"karokidii@gmail.com","login":"kd-11","name":"kd-11"},"msg":"rsx: Implement QUAD_STRIP\n- QUAD_STRIP evaluates to TRIANGLE_STRIP in memory. The memory layout is identical.\n- The only difference between the two modes would be the primitive_ID but that doesnt matter on RSX\n- Its worth noting that results will be different between the two modes if input vertices are non-coplanar for every set of N verts","sha":"fe5828cb478c180ae21b435fb851a9ee8aa13bee"}
