{"author":{"avatar":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15904127?v=4","date":"2020-01-06T21:48:58Z","email":"karokidii@gmail.com","login":"kd-11","name":"kd-11"},"committer":{"avatar":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15904127?v=4","date":"2020-01-07T12:56:54Z","email":"15904127+kd-11@users.noreply.github.com","login":"kd-11","name":"kd-11"},"msg":"video: Remove pointless aspect ratio option\n\n- The auto option is used when requesting the system is works like a\n\"dont care\" specifier to tell the system to use what settings have been\npassed in by HDMI EDID or the user TV type setting. Since this option\nsimulates the \"TV type setting\", auto makes no sense and is also not\nsomething you can select on a PS3.\n- Also adds a few missing checks.","sha":"ad845861be8190f3d6d08fb0df9e8a0bf84372db"}
