{"author":{"avatar":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15904127?v=4","date":"2020-01-13T17:46:58Z","email":"karokidii@gmail.com","login":"kd-11","name":"kd-11"},"committer":{"avatar":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15904127?v=4","date":"2020-01-14T11:32:40Z","email":"15904127+kd-11@users.noreply.github.com","login":"kd-11","name":"kd-11"},"msg":"vk: Restructure command queue flushing behavior to avoid deadlock\n\n- Queueing commands on the offloader is a good idea but unfortunately\npage faults can still happen causing a cyclic dependency and eventual\ndeadlock. Characterized by a vk::wait_for_event timed out error\naccompanied by severe hitching.\n\n- Drain the fault-able commands before pushing a submit operation to the\nqueue. If a fault is in progress, bypass the queue system and submit\nraw. Technically this is incorrect but there isn't much that can be\ndone about it right now.","sha":"8bbda3dedb87b26f9047362a56cb9f5a3ed9a032"}
