{"author":{"avatar":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18193363?v=4","date":"2020-09-05T17:16:03Z","email":"elad3356p@gmail.com","login":"elad335","name":"Eladash"},"committer":{"avatar":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6028184?v=4","date":"2020-09-05T19:23:55Z","email":"Nekotekina@users.noreply.github.com","login":"Nekotekina","name":"Ivan"},"msg":"SPU: Do not ignore pending PUT tranfers just becase GET may not be cache-line atomic\n\nThis is not the proper way to emulate non-atomic GET tranfers, as it makes it seems as if PUT atomic tranfers arent atomic. (TODO)\nIncomplete GET cache line accesses still do not verify data though.","sha":"e4abd3dc5a5e6c443dc52923f7e33c30f99361e9"}
